115 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H6
/P 88 0 R
/T (The objective of the Implement Client Script & UI Policy \(Incident\) project is to demonstrate how ServiceNow client-side controls can be used to enforce data integrity on Incident records. This implementation showcases how UI Policies and Client Scripts can dynamically make fields mandatory, auto-populate values, control field behavior, and prevent record submission when required conditions are not met. The solution ensures that Incidents are created with complete and valid information, improving data quality and consistency across the platform.)
/E (The objective of the Implement Client Script & UI Policy \(Incident\) project is to demonstrate how ServiceNow client-side controls can be used to enforce data integrity on Incident records. This implementation showcases how UI Policies and Client Scripts can dynamically make fields mandatory, auto-populate values, control field behavior, and prevent record submission when required conditions are not met. The solution ensures that Incidents are created with complete and valid information, improving data quality and consistency across the platform.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
